              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a scholarship, then the Telugu for to question."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: విద్య",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విద్య — vidya — \"education; learning\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ప్రతి పిల్లవాడికి విద్య అవసరం. prati pillavāḍiki vidya avasaraṁ. Every child needs education."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విద్యార్థి, a student, and విశ్వవిద్యాలయం, a university, which you know, are built on it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "విద్య (vidya) is borrowed from Sanskrit vidyā, \"knowledge\" (CDIAL 11741), from vid, \"to know\"; Telugu shortens the final long a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
